    {
      "id": "creation-reaches-its-collaborators-through-inversion",
      "contexts": [
        "creation"
      ],
      "statement": "Interactive Skill creation does not import the Contexts it collaborates with, and none of them imports it. Everything it needs from the reference, admission and trial Contexts arrives as a narrow interface injected by a composition root, so the creation loop can be replaced or removed without any other Context changing.",
      "examples": [
        "Enqueueing a creation job goes through an interface the wiring package supplies, not through the queue Context's own Service.",
        "A Context that wants to know what a creation session produced reads the Skill Version the session created, not the session.",
        "Credit and identity are reached the same way every other Context reaches them, because neither is part of the creation loop being kept replaceable."
      ],
